        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000008"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>sponges do not seem to have a mesoderm and accordingly Amphimedon lacks transcription factors involved in mesoderm development (Fkh, Gsc, Twist, Snail)[http://www.nature.com/nature/journal/v466/n7307/full/nature09201.html]. Mesoderm may not be homologous across verteberates</owl:annotatedTarget>
