        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000003"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A comparative anatomical approach reveals three apparent morphotypes of the cecal appendix, as well as appendix-like structures in some species that lack a true cecal appendix. Cladistic analyses indicate that the appendix has evolved independently at least twice (at least once in diprotodont marsupials and at least once in Euarchontoglires), shows a highly significant (P &lt; 0.0001) phylogenetic signal in its distribution, and has been maintained in mammalian evolution for 80 million years or longer.[well established][VHOG]</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:date_retrieved>2012-09-17</oboInOwl:date_retrieved>
        <oboInOwl:external_class>VHOG:0001306</oboInOwl:external_class>
