        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any of the coil glands of the skin that secrete sweat.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>TODO - check if all sweat glands are epidermal - see EMAPA:29743</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>A gland that secretes sweat, found in the dermis or subcutaneous tissue, opening by a duct on the body surface. [TFD][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>Sweat glands (also called sudoriferous glands) are unique to mammals.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>In humans a system of apocrine - and merocrine sweat glands is the main method of cooling. Many other mammals rely on panting or other means as a primary source of cooling, but still use sweat glands to aid in body temperature regulation</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
