        <obo:IAO_0000115>A (free) limb that is connected to a pectoral girdle. The extent of this structure includes autopod, stylopod and zeugopod regions when present, but excludes the pectoral girdle and its parts.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Note distinction between arm and forelimb. hand is part of forelimb, but not part of arm</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <obo:RO_0002171 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002103"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Upper limb, which connects the manus with the pectoral girdle.[AAO]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>note that this corresponds to FMA:&apos;free upper limb&apos; (a limb segment), NOT FMA:&apos;upper limb&apos;. Both MA and FMA consider shoulder (and shoulder bones) part of upper limb</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
