    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002372">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001961"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001555"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001735"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Either of the two small almond-shaped masses of lymph tissue found on either side of the oropharynx.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>the term &apos;tonsil&apos; can be ambiguous, sometimes refering specifically to the palatine tonsil, sometimes generically to include the cecal tonsils of avians. This class represents lymphoid tissue that is part of the tonsillar ring, in the mouth/throat region</obo:IAO_0000232>
