            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>That portion of the chorionic wall in the region of its uterine attachment, which gives rise to chorionic villi; it consists of the mesoderm that lines the chorionic vesicle and, on the maternal side, of the trophoblast that lines the intervillous spaces; in the last half of gestation, the mesodermal connective tissue is largely replaced by fibrinoid material, and the amnionic membrane is adherent to the fetal side of the plate.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BTO:0002879</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:31872</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
