        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Pharyngeal_pouch_(embryology)</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>XAO:0000282</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ZFA:0001106</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>branchial pouch</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>visceral pouch</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>pharyngeal pouches</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>visceral pouches</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0004117</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#efo_slim"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#human_subset"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#mouse_subset"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#pheno_slim"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#vertebrate_core"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The pouches are polarized structures. For example, whereas the rostral half of each pouch expresses Bmp-7, the caudal half expresses FGF-8 and the dorsal aspect of each pouch is marked via its expression of Pax-1. each pouch has an individual sense of identity. Shh expression is a prominent early feature of the caudal endoderm of the second arch, and individual pouches mark the anterior limits of expression of Hox genes within the pharyngeal endoderm; Hox-a2 has a rostral boundary at the second pouch, Hox-a3 at the third pouch and Hox-a4 at the most caudal pouch[PMID:16313389]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>pharyngeal pouch</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
