        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>A cervical thymus is a pathological structure in a human - it can form during the migration of the thymus to its location in the mediastinum. Some mice have a cervical thymus. There are examples of cervical thymi in marsupials and prosimians[ISBN:0781714125]</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
