        <obo:IAO_0000115>Subcutaneous adipose tissue that is located in the peritoneal cavity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Adipose tissue located inside the peritoneal cavity, packed in between internal organs and torso. An excess of visceral fat is known as central obesity, or belly fat, the pot belly or beer belly effect, in which the abdomen protrudes excessively[BTO:0004041].</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <terms:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473"/>
